Subject: [PATCH] fix(equipment): thirteen pages showed the photographs without
 saying what they are
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Caught by checking the built HTML rather than the source. tests/equipment.test.ts
asserted the disclosure by reading three files — the equipment index, the
equipment detail page, the diagnosis page — and passed. Meanwhile the "What
this job runs on" and "What this method runs on" blocks had been given
equipment thumbnails, rendered them across seven service pages and six method
pages, and carried no disclosure at all, because no test knew those files
existed.

That is the whole failure mode of a source-reading assertion: it can only check
the files somebody thought to name. So the real guard now lives in
scripts/audit-site.mjs, which walks all 404 prerendered pages and fails the
build on any page rendering an equipment image without one of the two
disclosure sentences. It cannot go stale, because the thing it inspects is the
thing the crawler receives.

The two source assertions stay as the cheap early warning — npm run verify runs
tests before build, so a developer sees it a minute sooner.

- 64/64 equipment images referenced in built HTML, across 29 pages
- 0 pages render one without a disclosure (was 13)
- 389 tests pass, audit clean, 404 pages
- 10 routes x 4 viewports, no horizontal overflow

